From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:26:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple-g5p: admit system sleep with a deferred close
 pending

A context that closes while the PM may still write its free list back
stays bound until a job of a third context runs (render-user-pmset.h).
With one compositor running that never happens: a client that ran at
boot and exited stays the PM's previous context for good, and system
sleep refused on it at every attempt. On J71t with labwc idle and the
firmware parked, every s2idle attempt drained for 1 s and then refused
("close-defer slots=8/7 ... pm=last" at boot, no "close-deferred"
after).

The hazard is a write-back on a later job. No job runs between the sleep
reservation and platform off: the client and host gates are shut, the
sleep detach unbinds every slot the firmware holds, and the resumed
firmware's PM starts with no last or previous context
(g5p_rv3_rebuild_host() clears both and every context's retained
binding). The pending close then releases after the next job with a
release plan, as after an in-boot recovery, never an unbind of old-epoch
slots.

Drop the deferred close from the sleep busy states. The R1 quiescent
certificate, the ring and stamp checks and every other busy state are
unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
index 6a89e5f48..6e3ab71c5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
@@ -8,6 +8,16 @@
  * when idle. *drains is set when the client drain in prepare can clear it
  * (work in flight); otherwise nothing at idle clears it and only a refusal is
  * honest.
+ *
+ * A deferred close (render-user-pmset.h) is not a reason: it keeps a closed
+ * context's slots bound while the PM may still write its free list back on a
+ * LATER job of the context that followed. No job runs between this
+ * reservation and platform off, the sleep detach unbinds every held slot, and
+ * the resumed firmware's PM starts with no last or previous context
+ * (g5p_rv3_rebuild_host()), so the pending close releases after resume like
+ * after an in-boot recovery. With one compositor running, a context that
+ * closed earlier stays "previous" for good, so refusing on it refused every
+ * sleep.
  */
 static const char *g5p_sleep_busy(struct g5p_drm *d, bool *drains)
 {
@@ -26,9 +36,6 @@ static const char *g5p_sleep_busy(struct g5p_drm *d, bool *drains)
 	/* A bind's DC3 pair the firmware never consumed; only a later DC op clears it. */
 	if (rd->dc_pending)
 		return "dc-pending";
-	/* Released only after a job of a third context (render-user-pmset.h). */
-	if (rd->close_deferred[0] || rd->close_deferred[1])
-		return "close-deferred";
 	*drains = true;
 	/* A lost-job drain or recovery may finish inside the client drain bound. */
 	if (rd->stuck)
